{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.11d4e8e1976eb5b2900022be.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The assessment concerns one fund at one identified distribution assessment time; listed closed-ended alternative asset funds are excluded.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.11d4e8e1976eb5b2900022be.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Direct exposure, indirect exposure and positive NAV are supplied as exact integers in the same valuation unit at that time, under a separately established aggregation methodology.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.11d4e8e1976eb5b2900022be.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Indirect exposure covers all relevant instruments and underlying private credit or private equity; the listed examples are not an exhaustive instrument whitelist.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.11d4e8e1976eb5b2900022be.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"A designation input records an actual SFC decision applicable at the assessment time; scrutiny, risk characteristics and home-regulator restrictions do not themselves establish designation.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.11d4e8e1976eb5b2900022be.a4","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The result answers whether a classification basis under this circular is present. It does not determine historical classification persistence, overall distribution compliance or legal approval.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":null,"candidate_id":"candidate.07d39f78c86a484da95f722841233011","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Does an in-scope Fund have a contemporaneous complex-product classification basis under this circular? True means aggregate direct and indirect private-market exposure is at least 50% of NAV or an operative SFC designation exists, requiring complex-product treatment on that basis. False means both bases are absent on established facts; it does not establish declassification following an earlier threshold crossing or non-complex status under other rules. Unknown inputs remain unknown unless an independently established branch determines the result. Out-of-scope funds receive no answer. This predicate confers no legal approval.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["time"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":[],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"Inspection of both prior models found that they already distinguish the relevant actors, underlying assets, intermediate instruments, fund-wide aggregation, exclusions and operative designation. No source-supported rival threshold rule was identified. The consequential remaining distinction is between a contemporaneous classification basis and an enduring classification status: a below-threshold snapshot without an operative designation does not resolve the effect of an earlier threshold crossing. Missing evidence also differs from evidence that a classification basis is absent. The proposal therefore retains the two classification routes while expressly limiting the question answered.","run_id":"run.08f45e4d9030408999f87203f067aefc","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"be86c12a28ac1c552b9cc386dfa44174629a63a786068d9bf5d8cdb44cbfa056","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u29.4630","d4148dd852cee.u32.4805","d4148dd852cee.u4.564","d4148dd852cee.u59.7979","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Contemporaneous fund-level classification basis for distribution"}